<title>USA: Central Financial Acceptance Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Central Financial Acceptance Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>COMMERCE, Calif. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Unaudited, in thousands)</p>
<p>							 Quarter Ended</p>
<p>							    March 31,</p>
<p>							1997	     1996</p>
<p> Total Revenue				 $12,657	  $ 7,232</p>
<p> Income before discontinued operations   1,807	    1,091</p>
<p> Income from discontinued operations (a)    --		 12</p>
<p>    Net income				   1,807	    1,103</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share before discontinued</p>
<p>  operations					0.25	     0.21</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share discontinued</p>
<p>  operations (a)				    --		 --</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share			     0.25	     0.21</p>
<p> Supplementary Earnings Per Share (b)     0.25	     0.19</p>
<p>(a) Reflects operations of Central Auto Sales Inc., which was sold for net book value to CFAC's parent company on Aug. 1, 1996.</p>
<p>(b) Based on 7,277,000 shares outstanding, as if all shares were outstanding as of Jan. 1, 1996, and gives effect to a reduction in interest expense resulting from the reduction of indebtedness upon application of the net proceeds of the company's initial public offering which was consummated on June 26, 1996, as if such offering had occurred on Jan. 1, 1996.</p>
